## Rules

1. **Do not inflate scores.** A 3 is fine. A 2 is fine. The point is honest differentiation.
2. **Do not use discovery call ratios as evidence.** The discovery program was skewed toward bio. All verticals are weighted equally.
3. **Cross-vertical events score higher** than single-vertical events at the same quality level, because they spread exposure without concentrating bets.
4. **Always check for stacking opportunities.** If the event is within a week and geography of another event (confirmed or pursuing), flag it.
5. **Speaking > sponsoring > booth > attending.** Always recommend pursuing speaking first. Only recommend sponsorship if the package includes stage time and the audience density justifies the cost.
6. **If the user provides a URL, fetch it first.** Do not score based on the name alone if you can get real details.
7. **Flag when an event is too late to act on.** If the event is <2 weeks away and requires a CFP submission or sponsorship negotiation, say so.
